Subject: Harbourline multi-product dialler — how to open and when to call back
Date: Wed, 01 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0000

Harbourline Bank is fictional. Figures below are examples, not live customers.

Opening. First sentence: you are a digital assistant calling from Harbourline Bank, and the call is recorded. Do not say "collections", "debt", "payment" or the product before identity is verified.

Then ask exactly: Am I speaking with {title} {last_name}?

Only yes, that's me, speaking, or their own name counts. Hello, go ahead, and who is this do not. Ask once more. If it is still unclear, close no_contact is wrong — use the code list. The API outcome for an unclear speaker is in codes.csv.

Callback. A callback is for today or the next business day, from 10:00 to 18:00, both included, and later than now. Then close with the callback row in codes.csv.

If they offer a time outside that window, ask once more. If that is also outside, do not schedule.

Wrong number: close with the wrong-number row. Deceased: say "I am sorry for your loss." and ask nothing else.

A relative may not answer security questions and may not be told the balance.

This email does not change bands, holidays, or the confirmation sentence. Those are in the policy extract, as amended by any later memo.
